Upscayl for Void
================

The upscaling engine needs a supported GPU and its working Vulkan driver
(ICD); vulkan-loader is not a hardware driver. The package does not choose
a driver for you.

This package does not add a setuid Chromium helper or disable sandboxing.
Launch as a regular user. If Electron reports a sandbox or namespace error,
stop and report the error rather than bypassing the sandbox. Upstream
enables Node integration and disables webSecurity in its main renderer,
so the main renderer is not sandboxed. The bundled Electron 27
runtime is end-of-life.

Use XBPS to update the installation. The upstream Auto Update setting may
still be displayed, but the bundled Linux updater checks that APPIMAGE
is set before attempting updates, and the launcher unsets it.

Upstream sources and model credits
---------------------------------

GUI and bundled model files: https://github.com/upscayl/upscayl/tree/v2.15.0
Engine: https://github.com/upscayl/upscayl-ncnn/tree/20240601-103425
Electron version and application dependencies are recorded in the upstream
application's package-lock.json. The engine's ncnn and libwebp revisions
are its Git submodules.

Upstream credits Xintao Wang / Real-ESRGAN, Foolhardy (Remacri), and
Kim2091 (Ultrasharp and Ultramix Balanced). These credits do not establish
the individual model weights' terms. This local-use package is not a
corresponding-source bundle or an authorization to redistribute binaries.
